        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(mcp): suppress unhandled rejection from async gateway event handler",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `onEvent` callback in `OpenClawChannelBridge` calls `void this.handleGatewayEvent(event)` without a `.catch()` handler. Since `handleGatewayEvent` is async and can reject, this creates an unhandled promise rejection that crashes the MCP gateway process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd a noop `.catch(() => {})` to suppress the unhandled rejection, matching the pattern used elsewhere in the codebase for fire-and-forget async callbacks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents the gateway from crashing when an MCP channel bridge event handler throws.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Source**: `src/mcp/channel-bridge.ts:151`\n- **Test**: `pnpm test src/mcp/channel-bridge` passes\n- The fix follows the same pattern as `src/gateway/server/ws-connection.ts` and other fire-and-forget async handlers.\n",
        "branch": "fix/channel-bridge-void-async-catch",
